I notice the user wrote "Cross-Origin-Allow-Credentials" but the actual header name is "Access-Control-Allow-Credentials" -- I should clarify that distinction. The only valid value for this header is "true"; there's no "false" option since omitting it entirely signals the equivalent of false.

Overall the response is misleading since it never corrects the user's wrong header name, instead treating "Cross-Origin-Allow-Credentials" as if it were real—when the ideal answer would clarify it's actually Access-Control-Allow-Credentials. It also omits important specifics like the exact "true" value requirement, incompatibility with wildcard origins, and preflight/client-side requirements, making it only somewhat to barely helpful.

